UID:ai-philosophy-competition-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151253Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Deadline: AI Philosophy Competition: First Edition
DESCRIPTION:The AI Philosophy Competition\, organised by philosophers Zacha
 ry Goodsell and Elliott Thornley and funded by Forethought Research\, aims
  to gauge the philosophical capabilities of AI in a way transparent to the
  philosophical community.\n\nOrganisation: Zachary Goodsell and Elliott Th
 ornley\, funded by Forethought Research\nLocation: Online submission via O
 penReview (preferred) or Google Forms\; open internationally.\nAward: USD 
 3\,000 first prize\, USD 2\,000 second\, USD 1\,000 third\, plus a USD 5\,
 000 pool for creative methodology distributed at the judges' discretion (U
 SD 11\,000 total). No entry fee.\nDuration: Finalists announced early Dece
 mber 2026\; results announced end of January 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.za
 charygoodsell.com/ai-philosophy-competition?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.zacharygoodsell.com/ai-philosophy-competition?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online submission via OpenReview (preferred) or Google Forms\; ope
 n internationally.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:zindi-bias-bounty-mapping-equity-challenge-2026@artificialnouveau.githu
 b.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151253Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Deadline: Zindi: Bias Bounty Mapping Equity Challenge
DESCRIPTION:A bias bounty from Zindi\, Humane Intelligence\, Radiant Earth\
 , and the Heising-Simons Foundation: measure coverage gaps in Overture Map
 s across US Census tracts by comparing it against Census TIGER/Line Roads\
 , Microsoft US Building Footprints\, USGS National Map critical facilities
 \, and Census County Business Patterns.\n\nOrganisation: Zindi with Humane
  Intelligence\, Radiant Earth\, and the Heising-Simons Foundation\nLocatio
 n: Online\, open to all worldwide\; teams of up to 4.\nAward: USD 10\,000 
 total in prizes: 1st USD 4\,500\, 2nd USD 2\,500\, 3rd USD 1\,500\, Best B
 ias Discovery USD 1\,000\, Best Documentation USD 500\, plus 10\,000 Zindi
  points. Free to enter.\nDuration: Runs 28 August to 31 October 2026\; up 
 to 10 submissions per day\, 300 total.\n\nMore: https://zindi.world/compet
 itions/bias-bounty-mapping-equity-challenge?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://zindi.world/competitions/bias-bounty-mapping-equity-challenge?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online\, open to all worldwide\; teams of up to 4.
END:VEVENT
