DTSTAMP:20261104T151253Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261102
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261103
SUMMARY:Deadline: ARC Prize 2026
DESCRIPTION:The ARC Prize Foundation runs its 2026 competition for progress
  toward artificial general intelligence\, with a USD 2\,000\,000 total pri
 ze pool across three tracks: the main Kaggle competition on the ARC-AGI-2 
 static reasoning benchmark\, a track on ARC-AGI-3 interactive agent reason
 ing (second milestone 30 September 2026)\, and a paper prize for research 
 that advances understanding of ARC-AGI...\n\nOrganisation: ARC Prize Found
 ation\nLocation: Online (Kaggle)\, worldwide\nAward: USD 2\,000\,000 total
  prize pool across three tracks (ARC-AGI-2\, ARC-AGI-3 agents\, and a pape
 r prize)\; milestone prizes include USD 25\,000 / 10\,000 / 2\,500\nDurati
 on: Competition runs through 2 November 2026 (paper track 8 November)\; re
 sults announced 4 December 2026\n\nMore: https://arcprize.org/competitions
 /2026?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://arcprize.org/competitions/2026?utm_source=artificialnouveaugran
 tdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online (Kaggle)\, worldwide
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:emaf-2027-call-for-entries@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151253Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261215
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261216
SUMMARY:Deadline: EMAF 2027: Call for Entries\, Film / Installation / Expan
 ded
DESCRIPTION:The European Media Art Festival (EMAF) in Osnabrueck invites su
 bmissions for its 2027 edition in three sections: Film (experimental films
  of all lengths and any theme)\, Installation (installative\, interactive\
 , spatial or sculptural media art works) and Expanded (performances\, live
  events or workshops).\n\nOrganisation: European Media Art Festival (EMAF)
 \nLocation: Osnabrueck\, Germany. Open worldwide\; selected artists are in
 vited to the festival with free accreditation\, three hotel nights and a c
 ontribution to travel costs.\nAward: All films in the International Select
 ion are equal winners of the EMAF Award and receive EUR 400 each. Screenin
 g fees: EUR 250 for Features\, EUR 80-250 for curated programmes depending
  on length\, EUR 500 for installations and expanded projects\; production 
 costs for installations and expanded projects are paid by the festival. Se
 lected artists get free accreditation\, three hotel nights (longer if setu
 p requires) and a travel cost contribution. No entry fee.\nDuration: Festi
 val in Osnabrueck\, spring 2027\; screening prints must arrive by 1 April 
 2027\n\nMore: https://emaf.filmchief.com/entry-forms?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://emaf.filmchief.com/entry-forms?utm_source=artificialnouveaugran
 tdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Osnabrueck\, Germany. Open worldwide\; selected artists are invite
 d to the festival with free accreditation\, three hotel nights and a contr
 ibution to travel costs.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oberhausen-73-call-for-films-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151253Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270118
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270119
SUMMARY:Deadline: Internationale Kurzfilmtage Oberhausen: Call for Films\, 
 73rd Festival (2027)
DESCRIPTION:The 73rd International Short Film Festival Oberhausen (27 April
  to 2 May 2027)\, one of the oldest and most influential short film festiv
 als\, opens its call for films across five competitions: International (ma
 x 35 minutes\, produced outside Germany\, German festival premiere require
 d)\, German (max 45 minutes\, produced in Germany\, no premiere requiremen
 t)\, NRW (max 45 minutes\, produced or...\n\nOrganisation: Internationale 
 Kurzfilmtage Oberhausen (International Short Film Festival Oberhausen)\nLo
 cation: Oberhausen\, Germany. International Competition open to production
 s from outside Germany (plus co-productions)\; separate German\, NRW\, Chi
 ldren's and Youth\, and MuVi competitions.\nAward: International Competiti
 on: Grand Prize of the City of Oberhausen EUR 8\,000\, Principal Prize EUR
  4\,000\, Promotional Prize EUR 1\,500\, plus a European Film Awards short
  film nomination. German Competition: EUR 5\,000 main prize\, EUR 1\,500 p
 romotional\, EUR 2\,500 3sat Emerging Talent Prize (with purchase offer)\,
  EUR 1\,000 ZONTA Prize for a female filmmaker. NRW Competition: EUR 1\,00
 0 and EUR 500 prizes\, plus NRW Ministry prizes of EUR 5\,000 and EUR 3\,0
 00\, FIPRESCI Prize\, EUR 2\,000 Ecumenical Jury Prize\, EUR 750 WDR Westa
 rt Audience Jury Prize. Children's and Youth: several EUR 1\,000-1\,500 pr
 izes and an ECFA Short Film Award nomination. Prizes go to the directors. 
 SUBMISSION FEE: first five submissions per submitter are free\; EUR 20 han
 dling fee per film from the sixth.\nDuration: Festival runs 27 April to 2 
 May 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.kurzfilmtage.de/en/festival/submission/?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.kurzfilmtage.de/en/festival/submission/?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Oberhausen\, Germany. International Competition open to production
 s from outside Germany (plus co-productions)\; separate German\, NRW\, Chi
 ldren's and Youth\, and MuVi competitions.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wow-wearableart-awards-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151253Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270211
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270212
SUMMARY:Deadline: World of WearableArt (WOW) Awards Competition 2027 (Welli
 ngton\, New Zealand)
DESCRIPTION:WOW is the world's largest wearable-art competition\, culminati
 ng in a staged show in Wellington\, New Zealand\, with the 2027 awards nig
 ht on 17 September 2027. The Kinetic and Avant-garde sections regularly at
 tract technology-driven wearables\, making this a natural target for e-tex
 tile\, robotic and sensor-driven garment work.\n\nOrganisation: World of W
 earableArt\nLocation: Wellington\, New Zealand\; open to designers worldwi
 de. Finished garments must be shipped to New Zealand (regional drop-off wi
 ndows mid-March to mid-May 2027).\nAward: Over NZD 200\,000 in prizes acro
 ss 25 awards. Per the published 2026 prize schedule: Supreme WOW Award NZD
  30\,000\, runner-up NZD 15\,000\, section winners NZD 8\,000 each. No ent
 ry fee.\nDuration: Annual competition\; entries open November 2026\, award
 s night 17 September 2027 in Wellington.\n\nMore: https://www.worldofweara
 bleart.com/competition/key-dates-and-deadlines?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.worldofwearableart.com/competition/key-dates-and-deadlines?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Wellington\, New Zealand\; open to designers worldwide. Finished g
 arments must be shipped to New Zealand (regional drop-off windows mid-Marc
 h to mid-May 2027).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:movies-that-matter-festival-2027-submissions@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20261104T151253Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: Movies that Matter Festival 2027: Film Submissions
DESCRIPTION:Movies that Matter\, the human rights film festival in The Hagu
 e (19-27 March 2027)\, is open for 2027 submissions. The festival screens 
 poignant fiction films and revealing documentaries that stir debates about
  human rights\, sustainability and the fight against injustice\, and feeds
  several competitions: the Grand Jury Documentary Competition (eight docum
 entaries\, EUR 5\,000\, winner eligible for...\n\nOrganisation: Movies tha
 t Matter\nLocation: The Hague\, Netherlands (festival 19-27 March 2027)\; 
 submissions open worldwide\, attendance not required for submission.\nAwar
 d: Cash prizes: EUR 5\,000 Grand Jury Documentary award (winner also becom
 es eligible for consideration for the Academy Award for Best Documentary F
 eature)\, EUR 5\,000 Grand Jury Fiction award\, and EUR 1\,500 Shorts awar
 d\; further competitions (Activist Lens\, Justice Frame\, Dutch Focus\, Ed
 ucation Award\, Audience Award) publish no amounts. SUBMISSION FEE: EUR 25
  until 30 September 2026\, EUR 35 late fee 1 October to 1 November 2026\; 
 fee waivers only in very exceptional cases.\n\nMore: https://moviesthatmat
 ter.nl/en/festival/industry/film-submissions/?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://moviesthatmatter.nl/en/festival/industry/film-submissions/?utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:The Hague\, Netherlands (festival 19-27 March 2027)\; submissions 
 open worldwide\, attendance not required for submission.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jmem-new-media-award-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151253Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261108
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261109
SUMMARY:Deadline: Judson-Morrissey Excellence in New Media Award 2026 (BIPO
 C students)
DESCRIPTION:The Judson-Morrissey Excellence in New Media Award (JMEM) is th
 e New Media Caucus's scholarship program supporting BIPOC students in new 
 media art fields. It gives multiple unrestricted monetary awards of up to 
 USD 500 each\, funded through donor contributions\, and features awardees 
 in an NMC Header/Footer Gallery exhibition and a digitally published inter
 view.\n\nOrganisation: New Media Caucus\nLocation: Online application\; th
 e New Media Caucus is an international nonprofit. Open to BIPOC undergradu
 ate and graduate students in new media art fields.\nAward: Multiple unrest
 ricted awards of varying amounts up to USD 500 each\, funded through donor
  contributions. Awardees are also featured in an NMC Header/Footer Gallery
  exhibition and a digitally published interview. Free to apply.\n\nMore: h
 ttps://newmediacaucus.org/opportunities/jmem-scholarship-open-call?utm_sou
 rce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://newmediacaucus.org/opportunities/jmem-scholarship-open-call?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online application\; the New Media Caucus is an international nonp
 rofit. Open to BIPOC undergraduate and graduate students in new media art 
 fields.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fondation-schneider-talents-contemporains-water-2026@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151253Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261122
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261123
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fondation Francois Schneider: Talents Contemporains 16th 
 Edition - Water
DESCRIPTION:The Fondation Francois Schneider's Talents Contemporains compet
 ition\, in its 16th edition\, supports contemporary creation on the theme 
 of WATER. Submissions can be a project for an installation or sculpture\, 
 or an existing unique work in painting\, drawing\, sculpture\, installatio
 n\, photography\, video\, textile art or other fine and visual arts\; perf
 orming arts and music are excluded.\n\nOrganisation: Fondation Francois Sc
 hneider\nLocation: Wattwiller\, France. Open internationally to visual art
 ists of all nationalities (legal age).\nAward: EUR 15\,000 per laureate (m
 erit prize plus acquisition of the work\; EUR 8\,000 when the work is part
  of a multiple edition\, e.g. photo or video)\; up to 7 laureates. Sculptu
 re and installation projects can additionally receive up to EUR 50\,000 in
  production assistance. No entry fee stated.\nDuration: Call open 23 Septe
 mber to 22 November 2026. Laureates get an exhibition at the foundation's 
 art centre in Wattwiller\, a bilingual publication\, entry into the collec
 tion and a video portrait.\n\nMore: https://www.fondationfrancoisschneider
 .org/en/contemporary-talents-competition/contemporary-talents-competition-
 water-wattwiller/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referra
 l
URL:https://www.fondationfrancoisschneider.org/en/contemporary-talents-comp
 etition/contemporary-talents-competition-water-wattwiller/?utm_source=arti
 ficialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Wattwiller\, France. Open internationally to visual artists of all
  nationalities (legal age).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:zoud-gamelab-finlit-game-jam-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151253Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261116
SUMMARY:Deadline: Zoud GameLab 2026: Global Game Jam financial-literacy jam
  (prize and funding pool up to USD 140\,000)
DESCRIPTION:Zoud GameLab is a month-long virtual game jam run by Global Gam
 e Jam and Zoud\, the UAE's national financial wellbeing initiative\, under
  the theme Make FinLit Fun. Participants build a game that integrates fina
 ncial literacy in a meaningful way\; this is part of the judging criteria\
 , and a scoring rubric is published on the jam page.\n\nOrganisation: Zoud
  (UAE National Financial Wellbeing and Sustainability Initiative) with Glo
 bal Game Jam\nLocation: Online\, worldwide. Open to participants aged 18 a
 nd over in any country\; solo developers\, teams of any size and studios.\
 nAward: Shared prize and development-support funding pool of up to USD 140
 \,000 across best overall game\, runner-up\, third place\, financial-liter
 acy impact\, regional perspective\, compelling gameplay and a Best Game fr
 om the UAE award\; individual prize amounts are not published. No entry fe
 e.\nDuration: Month-long online jam\, 15 October to 15 November 2026\; win
 ners announced December 2026.\n\nMore: https://itch.io/jam/zoud-gamelab?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://itch.io/jam/zoud-gamelab?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online\, worldwide. Open to participants aged 18 and over in any c
 ountry\; solo developers\, teams of any size and studios.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:in-development-asterisk-ai-developing-countries-essay-contest-2026@arti
 ficialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151253Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261231
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
SUMMARY:Deadline: In Development x Asterisk Essay Contest: How Will AI Affe
 ct Developing Countries? (USD 10\,000 top prize)
DESCRIPTION:An essay contest run by the development-economics publication I
 n Development and Asterisk Magazine on how transformative AI will affect l
 ow- and middle-income countries\, and how those countries might respond.\n
 \nOrganisation: In Development and Asterisk Magazine\, with a special priz
 e from the African Tech Futures Lab\nLocation: Worldwide\, online submissi
 on. Authors based in low- and middle-income countries particularly encoura
 ged.\nAward: Winner USD 10\,000 plus publication in Asterisk (print and on
 line) and In Development\; two runners-up USD 5\,000 each plus publication
  in Asterisk (online) and In Development\; two honourable mentions USD 2\,
 000 each. Separate African Tech Futures Lab prize of USD 2\,500 for the be
 st essay by an African national\, combinable with the main prizes. No entr
 y fee stated.\n\nMore: https://indevelopmentmag.substack.com/p/how-will-ai
 -affect-developing-countries?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
URL:https://indevelopmentmag.substack.com/p/how-will-ai-affect-developing-c
 ountries?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Worldwide\, online submission. Authors based in low- and middle-in
 come countries particularly encouraged.
END:VEVENT
